+# PicoMarQ 1.1.0 validation
+
+The source and Windows bundle were prepared from the same build. The existing
+AppData profile selection is unchanged. Each recovered document becomes an
+independent native window, and each renderer can update only its own document.
+
+## Completed checks
+
+- `npm run build`: TypeScript and production Vite build pass.
+- `npm test`: 24 tests pass, including independent document recovery merges,
+  atomic saving, external-edit conflicts, backup recovery, old-profile handling,
+  context menus, Markdown escapes, and smart typography.
+- `npm run test:desktop`: passes in the actual Electron 44.6.0 application on
+  Linux with Xvfb. Covers the existing compact layout and editing controls;
+  separate windows for New/Open; duplicate Open protection; cross-window native
+  clipboard and independent undo; shared settings; simultaneous recovery;
+  Revert cancellation, failed reads, disk reload, stable document identity, and
+  undo reset; duplicate Save As; multiple/relative subsequent-launch paths;
+  individual Save/Discard/Cancel and cancelled Save As; deferred Discard during
+  Exit; crash recovery; individual selection, scroll and window bounds;
+  restoration after Exit; last-window close; and migration of an existing v1
+  AppData profile including an unsaved untitled draft.
+- `npm run test:typography`: passes in Electron, including both editing views,
+  settings, the Heading 4 style, and whole-document conversions and undo.
+- `npm run test:equivalence`: 64 documents and 3,392 edited states compared;
+  81 documents round-trip. Parsing, serialization, word counts and highlighting
+  match the reference behavior.
+
+## Platform coverage
+
+The Windows x64 runtime is Electron's official 44.6.0 release, downloaded with
+checksum verification. The packaging script verifies executable code/data and
+resources when applying PicoMarQ's name, icon and version. The Windows ZIP
+contains the runtime and needs no installer or separately installed Node.js.
+
+Windows execution, Windows-native dialogs, Windows font enumeration and actual
+Explorer/default-app launches have not been run in this Linux environment.
+Subsequent-launch routing is exercised through Electron's real event handler;
+the operating-system association itself still needs a Windows bench check.
+
+## Build and packaging
+
+See README.md. The Windows ZIP extracts to a `PicoMarQ` folder. Close all old
+windows before replacing an existing application folder's contents. No AppData
+files are included in the ZIP or changed by copying the application files.
